  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific connected El Faro compound: both individually angled mapped 160m shafts, pale punched-window concrete frames, dark glazed inner strips/stepped upper storeys, closed roofs and pale louvered crowns, mapped high connector and two picture-led intermediate bridges, bounded entry canopies. Four existing shared concrete/window-grid/paint/membrane graphs. No neighboring high-rises, whole-block podium, ground-covering platform, copied signs/photo atlas, furnished interiors or construction cranes.",
    "identityBasis": "Q526622 retained reference lies within the distinctive pair. Standard Protomaps20261014 buildings35184495506605/35184628893115 (OSMways123417773/256804283) have separate rotated rectangles and160m values, connected by building_part35184628893116 (way256804284) at min_height147/height153. Ordinary front/reverse pictures identify this connected pair. These native geometries control the two separate orientations and bridge, not a generic twin box. Live OSM tags were rate limited and no exact live Wikidata-tag check is claimed. Fine facade allocation retains20degree/2m approximation.",
    "heightBasis": "Both native shafts are160m; the mapped upper connector spans147..153m. Native height provenance is unqualified, not a survey. Picture-led main concrete elevation128m, upper glazing155m, louvered crowns160m, fine windows/floor pitch3.1m and two lower links at79..81.4m/112..114.4m are visualization estimates. Lower connector inventory/heights and hidden reverse facade details remain explicitly approximate; no surveyed floor count or interior circulation is claimed.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original6m standard Mapzen ground/native roads/water and every independent surrounding building. Replace only the two native El Faro shafts and their mapped high connector. Own bounded buried feet meet coarse grade with separate tower floor datums; narrow entry canopies stay attached to their own shafts. No whole-block podium, broad slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Native terrain/water levels are not surveyed foundation/flood measurements.",
